1
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,960
This is really neat!

2
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,740
When do we eat?

3
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:20,420
First, we have to catch some fish.

4
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:27,650
In order to catch fish, you have to do this.

5
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,140
Here we go.

6
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:34,420
That's it.

7
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,160
Then drop it into the water.

8
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:41,150
All of this comes before eating. OK?

9
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,810
How do you know so much about fishing?

10
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:45,650
Grandpa taught me.

11
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,560
We spent a lot of time fishing together.

12
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:58,630
Now, the important thing is to get the hook close to the fish.

13
00:00:58,630 --> 00:00:59,620
All right?

14
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:08,680
Like this.

15
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,920
I think I see some fish right under us, Dad.

16
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:12,890
Oh, not a chance!

17
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:15,590
I just saw a big one!

18
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:16,570
Hi, there!

19
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:17,520
Hi.

20
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,220
What's your name?

21
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:19,620
Albert.

22
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:20,580
Are you all alone?

23
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,420
Yes, sir.

24
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,920
How old are you, Albert?

25
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,490
I'm ten.

26
00:01:27,490 --> 00:01:29,050
Where's your father?

27
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:33,720
He's up there at the lodge.

28
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,220
Does he know you're here?

29
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,960
Yes, sir.

30
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:40,150
OK, Robbie, maybe you should watch him.

31
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:42,060
The water's pretty deep here.

32
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:50,660
I'll watch him, Dad.

33
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,510
What time is it?

34
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:56,150
It's almost lunchtime, and no fish yet.

35
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:58,880
I can go up to the lodge for some hot dogs and drinks.

36
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,100
No way!

37
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,450
We're here to catch our lunch.

38
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:06,580
To catch fish, you need the right magic.

39
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,400
That's right.

40
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:07,990
I forgot!

41
00:02:07,990 --> 00:02:09,710
The right magic.

42
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:11,380
Do it for Robbie, Dad.

43
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,310
You remember?

44
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:13,510
Sure. Come on.

45
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:18,490
Well, first, you have to turn your hat around like this.

46
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:23,390
Then you close your eyes and say the magic words.

47
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:32,290
Fish, fish, send me a fish.

48
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:39,290
Fish, fish, send me a fish.... I got one!

49
00:02:39,290 --> 00:02:41,290
See, it works!

50
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,390
It's a big one!

51
00:02:42,390 --> 00:02:45,150
Well, it always worked for me, too.

52
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:55,320
Grandpa, get the net, please!

53
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,840
Dad, you got one, too!

54
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,130
You bet I have!

55
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:04,500
Easy, Philip, easy.

56
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:07,530
Sorry, Dad.

57
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:13,240
Well, one more and I've got a pair of boots.

58
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,110
You didn't say the magic words.

59
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:16,520
Robbie's right.

60
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:19,360
Yes, but you did, and we've got our lunch.

61
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,880
Let's build a fire and cook it!

62
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:23,320
Come on, Albert, you can help us!

63
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,080
I want to stay here and fish.

64
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:37,930
All right, but be careful.

65
00:03:37,930 --> 00:03:39,110
Is it finished yet?

66
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:40,050
I think so.

67
00:03:40,050 --> 00:03:44,350
I hope you like your fish well done.

68
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:46,310
Burned, you mean.

69
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:58,420
Hey, I'm a doctor, not a chef.

70
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:01,720
Help! Help! I can't swim!

71
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:04,920
Dad! Grandpa! He fell in!

72
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:06,450
Easy does it, Robbie.

73
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:22,440
That a boy.

74
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,930
That's it.

75
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:27,360
He's not breathing, Philip!

76
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,270
Robbie, run to the car!

77
00:04:29,270 --> 00:04:30,450
Bring a blanket and my medical bag.

78
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:32,500
Yes, Dad.

79
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:43,610
Now, come on, son. Come on, son.

80
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:46,610
Breathe, Albert!
